1
00:00:08,299 --> 00:00:11,177
‎MACHI MORI - CUSTOMS OFFICIAL

2
00:00:12,804 --> 00:00:16,433
Amazing! It's like
we stepped inside the painting.

3
00:00:18,810 --> 00:00:24,399
Strong, vivid colors
that envelop the entire body.

4
00:00:24,983 --> 00:00:29,112
-In short, basically, well…
-It's the best, right?

5
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:30,780
Yes.

6
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:33,450
It's the best.

7
00:00:34,034 --> 00:00:36,411
That reminds me.
Why did you invite me here?

8
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:40,790
You told me before
that you were interested in digital art.

9
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:43,543
That's sweet.

10
00:00:45,336 --> 00:00:47,881
But Mori, don't you ever go
on dates with a boyfriend?

11
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:49,174
A boyfriend?

12
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:52,177
A date?

13
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:55,263
Are you just not interested in romance?

14
00:00:55,346 --> 00:00:56,806
Romance.

15
00:00:56,890 --> 00:01:00,435
Love and affection?

16
00:01:01,686 --> 00:01:02,604
I am interested in it.

17
00:01:03,229 --> 00:01:04,397
You are, huh?

18
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:06,816
So, what's your type, then?

19
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:10,862
However, I have yet to define
what romance is.

20
00:01:10,945 --> 00:01:14,032
Who cares about the definition?

21
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:15,033
Love.

22
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:18,703
What is it, I wonder.

23
00:01:22,665 --> 00:01:26,085
‎There is major rainfall tonight

24
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:28,630
‎in Tokyo Prefecture
‎and Kanagawa Prefecture.

25
00:01:28,713 --> 00:01:31,549
‎It is also highly likely
‎there has already been flooding…

26
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:33,968
Oh man! Oh man!

27
00:01:34,677 --> 00:01:36,346
Hey, you're soaked!

28
00:01:36,429 --> 00:01:38,306
It's a total downpour outside!

29
00:01:38,389 --> 00:01:40,558
The link bridge has a lot of water
flowing through it.

30
00:01:40,642 --> 00:01:42,769
The drainage can't keep up at all.

31
00:01:42,852 --> 00:01:44,604
Dang, it's flooding?

32
00:01:44,687 --> 00:01:46,272
This area was built in a rush after all.

33
00:01:46,356 --> 00:01:47,440
Ah, thank you.

34
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:51,277
Let's just go home. All flights
must be canceled now, right?

35
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,656
Yes?

36
00:01:56,699 --> 00:01:57,617
Yes.

37
00:01:59,619 --> 00:02:03,331
Flight UNT815 from the Unitia Federation
will be landing shortly.

38
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:05,875
-What?
-Seriously? In this rain?

39
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:08,837
-The captain really did their best.
-This is the last flight of the day.

40
00:02:08,920 --> 00:02:10,839
Yes, let's wrap it up smoothly
and go home!

41
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:14,717
Is love…

42
00:02:18,012 --> 00:02:20,265
a torrential downpour?

43
00:02:20,348 --> 00:02:21,474
You're still thinking about that?

44
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:24,561
Hurry, let's go.

45
00:02:24,644 --> 00:02:25,645
Yes.

46
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:36,114
Just this way.

47
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:38,533
-Two booths, open.
-Please don't rush.

48
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:39,576
So next in line, please.

49
00:02:39,659 --> 00:02:41,995
-Please be careful.
-Just this way.

50
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:44,539
-It's okay. Don't worry.
-Next in line, please.

51
00:02:44,622 --> 00:02:47,208
Please watch your step.

52
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:49,168
This way, please.

53
00:02:49,252 --> 00:02:51,045
-Please watch your step.
-Let's go.

54
00:02:55,091 --> 00:02:56,217
Japanese is fine.

55
00:02:56,301 --> 00:02:58,386
He's third-generation Japanese.

56
00:02:58,469 --> 00:03:01,806
Speaks fluent Japanese too, right?

57
00:03:01,890 --> 00:03:03,892
We're engaged.

58
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:05,727
We're traveling before our wedding.

59
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:08,146
I see. Well then, your passports, please.

60
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:09,147
-Here.
-Thank you.

61
00:03:09,731 --> 00:03:11,441
-I'll just hold it to the glass.
-Be gentle.

62
00:03:11,524 --> 00:03:12,400
-We'll need it later.
-Yes.

63
00:03:12,483 --> 00:03:14,527
-Wonderful.
-Wonderful.

64
00:03:14,611 --> 00:03:17,363
Leon Araki and Aoi Onodera.

65
00:03:17,447 --> 00:03:20,325
Leon, you are visiting for tourism.

66
00:03:20,408 --> 00:03:21,576
How long is your stay?

67
00:03:23,369 --> 00:03:25,622
Wherever the wind blows,
wherever the stones call.

68
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:26,539
IMMIGRATION OFFICER, MINISTRY OF JUSTICE
AKIHIKO SEIKE

69
00:03:26,623 --> 00:03:29,334
-Stones?
-He is a gem appraiser.

70
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:30,877
He travels all around the world.

71
00:03:31,961 --> 00:03:35,173
I run a jewelry company myself,

72
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:37,675
so we really hit it off.

73
00:03:37,759 --> 00:03:39,552
-We did.
-We did!

74
00:03:39,636 --> 00:03:42,889
And then, I found a gem named Aoi.

75
00:03:43,973 --> 00:03:46,226
Stop it, Leon.

76
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:49,729
Look, this is the engagement ring
he gave me.

77
00:03:49,812 --> 00:03:51,731
How wonderful.

78
00:03:51,814 --> 00:03:53,149
So, how long is your stay?

79
00:03:53,983 --> 00:03:56,527
-About two weeks, right?
-Ah, yes.

80
00:03:56,611 --> 00:03:57,862
I guess so.

81
00:03:57,946 --> 00:04:00,573
Excuse me. I'll inspect your luggage now.

82
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:01,574
Yes.

83
00:04:05,495 --> 00:04:08,581
Is that also a form of love?

84
00:04:09,958 --> 00:04:11,042
Pardon?

85
00:04:11,125 --> 00:04:12,293
KEIICHIRO HAYAMI - IMMIGRATION OFFICIAL

86
00:04:17,131 --> 00:04:21,010
-What is this?
-That is a fountain pen.

87
00:04:21,094 --> 00:04:22,971
Adorned with gold and natural gems,

88
00:04:23,054 --> 00:04:26,474
passed down from the former
royal family of the Unitia Federation.

89
00:04:28,977 --> 00:04:30,019
Here you go.

90
00:04:31,437 --> 00:04:34,941
Excuse me, but approximately
how much is it worth?

91
00:04:36,901 --> 00:04:39,696
High-value items
may be subject to taxation.

92
00:04:40,863 --> 00:04:44,534
Oh, well, you cannot put a price tag
on something like this.

93
00:04:45,493 --> 00:04:47,161
That's not what I mean.

94
00:04:47,245 --> 00:04:50,164
-What?
-The interior work is falling behind.

95
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,583
We have less than a year
until the opening, you know?

96
00:04:53,376 --> 00:04:56,379
Miss, please refrain from having
phone calls in the inspection area.

97
00:04:57,171 --> 00:04:59,507
Send me the progress report later.

98
00:05:06,347 --> 00:05:08,641
I've seen her before.

99
00:05:08,725 --> 00:05:10,768
That's Toko Tsuzuki, the entrepreneur.

100
00:05:11,436 --> 00:05:15,106
She's super talented.
She made her mark revitalizing hotels.

101
00:05:29,537 --> 00:05:31,873
You are Ms. Toko Tsuzuki

102
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:42,633
I plan to get my medical license
in Japan, so…

103
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:45,678
He is a resident doctor
in the Unitia Federation.

104
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:48,264
Do you have documents
from your place of study?

105
00:05:48,347 --> 00:05:49,432
Ah, yes.

106
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:54,395
Thank you.

107
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:55,646
Go ahead.

108
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:57,732
-I will inspect your luggage.
-Okay.

109
00:05:58,441 --> 00:05:59,567
All right.

110
00:05:59,650 --> 00:06:01,027
-Thank you.
-Thanks.

111
00:06:01,986 --> 00:06:04,739
-Now, please head over there.
-Okay.

112
00:06:08,242 --> 00:06:10,036
Ah, sorry, one at a time.

113
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:15,792
One more time.

114
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:18,002
Um…

115
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:20,922
-What are these?
-Vitamins.

116
00:06:21,005 --> 00:06:24,509
He says they're good
for health and beauty.

117
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:26,803
Those are only supplements.

118
00:06:26,886 --> 00:06:30,139
Do you have the original container
that shows the ingredients?

119
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:32,934
I threw it away.

120
00:06:33,601 --> 00:06:36,479
We will need to confirm if these
are permitted entry into the country.

121
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:38,981
Excuse me.

122
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:41,859
I also have a few things
I'd like to confirm about Mr. Luca.

123
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:43,194
Let's step into the secondary room.

124
00:06:43,986 --> 00:06:44,946
The secondary room?

125
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:47,156
Sorry for the trouble.
Take them to the secondary room.

126
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,407
Okay.

127
00:06:48,491 --> 00:06:50,159
I'll carry your bags.

128
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:53,663
Excuse me.

129
00:06:53,746 --> 00:06:56,124
I need to get back to the office soon.

130
00:07:03,631 --> 00:07:05,299
Um, please hurry.

131
00:07:05,383 --> 00:07:07,093
Yes, yes, this way.

132
00:07:07,677 --> 00:07:09,178
Hurry! You too, Luca!

133
00:07:16,477 --> 00:07:17,812
What's that?

134
00:07:22,733 --> 00:07:24,235
You found it.

135
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:31,284
Toko.

136
00:07:31,909 --> 00:07:34,871
I was going to give this
to you in private, but…

137
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:40,543
Could that be…

138
00:07:40,626 --> 00:07:42,753
-No way, a proposal?
-Right here?

139
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:45,089
Oh my.

140
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:54,932
Toko, my love,

141
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:57,393
you've always been there for me.

142
00:07:57,935 --> 00:08:00,229
Now I want to be there for you.

143
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:03,065
Will you marry me?

144
00:08:05,401 --> 00:08:07,778
-Whoa!
-What happened?

145
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:09,947
Please stay calm!
Power will be restored shortly!

146
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:12,200
Please do not move from where you are!

147
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:13,534
POWER OUTAGE

148
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:16,078
EMERGENCY POWER

149
00:08:16,162 --> 00:08:17,246
Toko?

150
00:08:19,457 --> 00:08:21,083
Let go of me!

151
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:23,085
-What are you doing?
-Stay back!

152
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:24,253
Don't get any closer.

153
00:08:24,337 --> 00:08:26,631
Fine! Please calm down.

154
00:08:26,714 --> 00:08:28,799
-Come on!
-Everyone, please back away!

155
00:08:28,883 --> 00:08:30,134
-Get back!
-Everyone, get back!

156
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:31,677
-Get back!
-Let's calm down.

157
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:33,763
-Get back!
-Gate 24 Inspection Booth,

158
00:08:33,846 --> 00:08:35,473
a man has restrained a female passenger.

159
00:08:36,641 --> 00:08:38,643
Come on. Get back!

160
00:08:41,938 --> 00:08:43,564
Wait…

161
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:45,066
-Wait…
-Toko!

162
00:08:45,149 --> 00:08:46,984
Hey, hey, hey! Get back.

163
00:08:47,068 --> 00:08:48,110
That's my fountain pen! Excuse me…

164
00:08:48,194 --> 00:08:49,570
-Give that back!
-Stop!

165
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:51,155
-Get back!
-Stop!

166
00:08:52,406 --> 00:08:53,658
You little…

167
00:08:56,953 --> 00:08:58,079
Hayami!

168
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:02,375
No one come in!

169
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:04,710
Next time, I'll really stab someone!

170
00:09:07,421 --> 00:09:10,132
-Are you okay?
-Thank you.

171
00:09:10,675 --> 00:09:12,802
You're a doctor, right?

172
00:09:12,885 --> 00:09:14,845
-Could you examine him?
-Sure.

173
00:09:14,929 --> 00:09:15,846
Don't move!

174
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:18,849
I don't trust you.

175
00:09:19,725 --> 00:09:20,935
Gunji.

176
00:09:21,602 --> 00:09:22,853
How did you find me here?

177
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:26,232
D-Do you know each other?

178
00:09:27,525 --> 00:09:31,237
He's a former coworker.

179
00:09:31,946 --> 00:09:33,656
Ex-boyfriend.

180
00:09:35,449 --> 00:09:36,409
Right?

181
00:09:38,369 --> 00:09:40,413
I came here to protect you.

182
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:42,248
Because

183
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:44,500
I still love you.

184
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:51,007
Is this also…

185
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,051
love?

186
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:04,979
The meeting just ended.

187
00:10:05,062 --> 00:10:07,189
The airport director is here too.

188
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:09,066
Please tell me the situation.

189
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:12,111
The man is Ryosuke Gunji.
Using a fountain pen, he has taken

190
00:10:12,194 --> 00:10:14,697
two passengers and two staff hostage
and barricaded himself in.

191
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:16,032
Passengers are being held hostage.

192
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:17,533
What about the other passengers?

193
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:20,202
We evacuated them to the waiting area.

194
00:10:20,286 --> 00:10:22,622
-However…
-The link bridge is flooded,

195
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:24,290
so reinforcements can't make it through.

196
00:10:24,373 --> 00:10:26,751
My valuable fountain pen is in there!

197
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:28,210
Get it back quickly!

198
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,087
-Please calm down.
-Leon!

199
00:10:34,383 --> 00:10:37,845
A tactical unit is heading your way now.

200
00:10:37,928 --> 00:10:39,972
However, due to the heavy rain,

201
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:42,141
it will take them about an hour to arrive.

202
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:43,517
That long?

203
00:10:44,018 --> 00:10:45,269
What about Chief Hearing Officer Fukazawa?

204
00:10:45,353 --> 00:10:47,730
He's at the main Immigration Bureau
and can't reach you.

205
00:10:47,813 --> 00:10:48,981
Neither can we.

206
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:52,693
Until reinforcements arrive,
the remaining personnel must hold out.

207
00:10:52,777 --> 00:10:54,028
Understood.

208
00:10:54,779 --> 00:10:55,988
One hour.

209
00:10:57,114 --> 00:10:59,408
So this place will be
an isolated island until then?

210
00:10:59,492 --> 00:11:01,744
‎GATE24-SECONDARY ROOM

211
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:10,252
Don't answer that! Decline it!

212
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:11,921
Okay, okay.

213
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:13,756
Stop yelling at every little thing.

214
00:11:14,298 --> 00:11:16,634
-Are you all right, Luca?
-Hey, move away!

215
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:19,553
-Stop cuddling up.
-What's the problem?

216
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:22,181
Hey, hey! Don't move.

217
00:11:22,264 --> 00:11:24,308
May I clean up the luggage?

218
00:11:25,684 --> 00:11:28,396
We should take care of the belongings.

219
00:11:28,479 --> 00:11:29,397
Hey…

220
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,981
-Mori…
-Hayami.

221
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:34,568
It will take one hour
for the tactical unit to arrive.

222
00:11:34,652 --> 00:11:37,530
Please hold out until then.

223
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:55,923
Hey, you!

224
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:59,427
Gunji. You're Gunji, aren't you?

225
00:12:00,428 --> 00:12:02,346
Would you please talk to us?

226
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:05,641
We are not your enemies.

227
00:12:05,724 --> 00:12:09,019
Our top priority is for everyone
to get out of here safely.

228
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:12,731
I hear you're a former coworker
of Tsuzuki.

229
00:12:15,651 --> 00:12:16,735
Five years ago,

230
00:12:17,653 --> 00:12:20,072
we started a company together.

231
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:23,075
But as soon as it got on track,
she kicked me out,

232
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:24,660
claiming "differences in direction".

233
00:12:26,370 --> 00:12:29,582
-So you're doing this out of revenge?
-No!

234
00:12:30,249 --> 00:12:33,169
Someone from the old company
reached out to me.

235
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:36,922
They said the CEO was recently obsessing
over a young foreigner.

236
00:12:37,798 --> 00:12:40,426
-You mean me?
-That's right.

237
00:12:40,509 --> 00:12:41,886
When did you start seeing this guy?

238
00:12:41,969 --> 00:12:46,015
A year ago, when she came
to Unitia on business.

239
00:12:46,974 --> 00:12:49,018
I suddenly felt unwell,

240
00:12:49,101 --> 00:12:51,604
and Luca, who happened to be
passing by, took care of me.

241
00:12:52,938 --> 00:12:54,899
A fateful meeting, you could call it.

242
00:12:56,025 --> 00:12:57,359
What fate?

243
00:12:58,777 --> 00:13:01,864
A young, handsome doctor
who just happened to be passing by?

244
00:13:01,947 --> 00:13:03,073
Who's madly in love with you?

245
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:07,077
-How could anything be that convenient?
-It actually happened.

246
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:08,954
What?

247
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:12,291
-Are you jealous?
-No, I am not.

248
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:13,918
Let me tell you clearly.

249
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:16,795
This guy is a marriage fraudster!

250
00:13:17,713 --> 00:13:19,381
A marriage fraudster?

251
00:13:19,465 --> 00:13:21,175
That's the only explanation.

252
00:13:21,258 --> 00:13:22,760
What he's after is money.

253
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:25,596
That and status to live in Japan.

254
00:13:25,679 --> 00:13:27,014
What are you talking about?

255
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:29,266
Things like that happen, right?

256
00:13:29,808 --> 00:13:33,020
Well, yes. There are cases
where foreign nationals

257
00:13:33,103 --> 00:13:36,065
attempt to illegally obtain residency
through fake marriages.

258
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:38,275
-See?
-However,

259
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:41,487
marriage does not automatically
guarantee permission to live in Japan.

260
00:13:41,570 --> 00:13:43,531
The actual reality of the marriage
and the couple's lives

261
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:45,241
are strictly examined.

262
00:13:46,242 --> 00:13:47,159
Then

263
00:13:47,826 --> 00:13:50,621
perform that examination
right now, right here!

264
00:13:51,705 --> 00:13:52,540
Pardon?

265
00:13:52,623 --> 00:13:55,334
Expose the fact that this guy
is deceiving Toko.

266
00:13:55,417 --> 00:13:56,460
Until that's made clear,

267
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:59,088
no one leaves this room!

268
00:13:59,964 --> 00:14:01,340
Examining…

269
00:14:02,716 --> 00:14:04,301
love?

270
00:14:04,885 --> 00:14:07,388
Luca is a scammer?

271
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:10,808
And we have to examine it here?

272
00:14:13,769 --> 00:14:15,688
-The police, the police!
-Is it the tactical unit?

273
00:14:16,438 --> 00:14:17,731
They're here already?

274
00:14:26,448 --> 00:14:29,159
There, there, there!

275
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:34,123
Ah, finally made it.

276
00:14:34,206 --> 00:14:35,499
-Iuchi?
-What? Yes.

277
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:37,626
Huh? Where's the tactical unit?

278
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:40,337
Not here yet. Only the two of us
were able to move ahead.

279
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:43,424
Sorry, but we aren't here as your backup.

280
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:46,552
-What?
-We were in the airport

281
00:14:46,635 --> 00:14:48,721
investigating a separate matter.

282
00:14:49,513 --> 00:14:50,472
We got a tip-off.

283
00:14:50,556 --> 00:14:53,893
There's a possibility a marriage fraudster
is on this final flight.

284
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:57,855
Mori, what are you doing?

285
00:14:57,938 --> 00:14:59,523
Inspecting.

286
00:15:01,859 --> 00:15:05,112
Um, immigration is not a marriage agency,

287
00:15:05,195 --> 00:15:06,822
nor can we evaluate human affection.

288
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:10,326
Just investigate him! He's a scammer!

289
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:14,204
Fine!

290
00:15:14,955 --> 00:15:17,875
-If he insists, why not investigate?
-Um, like I said…

291
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:20,336
You saw it earlier, didn't you?
Luca's proposal.

292
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:22,546
That right there is proof of love.

293
00:15:24,798 --> 00:15:26,258
Proof of love.

294
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:42,733
Toko, let me tell you this again.

295
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:47,613
-Will you--
-Don't do it now!

296
00:15:47,696 --> 00:15:48,989
Um…

297
00:15:49,573 --> 00:15:50,741
Excuse me.

298
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:55,537
That blue stone…

299
00:15:56,372 --> 00:15:57,414
It's a sapphire.

300
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,541
I thought it'd look good on her.

301
00:16:00,626 --> 00:16:02,586
May I take a look at it?

302
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:07,883
What are you doing?

303
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:15,432
What are you doing?

304
00:16:16,558 --> 00:16:20,104
I can see a few tiny air bubbles
inside the stone.

305
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:21,188
Air bubbles?

306
00:16:21,271 --> 00:16:24,149
Natural sapphires contain inclusions.

307
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:26,944
However, having multiple
air bubbles like this

308
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:29,238
is a characteristic
commonly seen in glass.

309
00:16:29,321 --> 00:16:31,198
Then that stone is…

310
00:16:31,281 --> 00:16:32,783
I cannot say for certain,

311
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:36,662
but it may be a piece of glass,
made to imitate a sapphire.

312
00:16:38,122 --> 00:16:39,456
A fake?

313
00:16:41,166 --> 00:16:42,584
Is it this guy?

314
00:16:43,210 --> 00:16:44,378
See?

315
00:16:44,461 --> 00:16:46,964
He tried to trick you with a cheap ring!

316
00:16:47,047 --> 00:16:49,425
It hasn't been proven fake yet.

317
00:16:50,009 --> 00:16:52,803
Besides, the price doesn't matter.

318
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:55,597
As long as his feelings
are genuine, that's enough.

319
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,475
Um…

320
00:16:58,559 --> 00:17:02,938
Actually, there is
one more thing that concerns me.

321
00:17:03,522 --> 00:17:05,149
-One more thing?
-Yes.

322
00:17:05,232 --> 00:17:08,152
Earlier, the woman at the adjacent booth

323
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:10,738
was wearing a similar ring.

324
00:17:12,698 --> 00:17:15,451
-The woman next to us too?
-Yes.

325
00:17:16,076 --> 00:17:17,453
Were you aware of this?

326
00:17:19,204 --> 00:17:22,124
I don't know. Maybe it's a coincidence.

327
00:17:22,708 --> 00:17:24,460
That couple too?

328
00:17:25,169 --> 00:17:28,213
True, it is a similar ring.

329
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:30,466
Now that you mention it, I saw something.

330
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:32,801
During the proposal earlier.

331
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:40,267
Luca and Leon?

332
00:17:41,393 --> 00:17:43,479
Those two might know each other.

333
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:45,814
Iuchi.

334
00:17:47,524 --> 00:17:48,400
Could you folks

335
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:51,403
help us out a bit?

336
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:57,493
Leon.

337
00:17:57,576 --> 00:17:58,744
A conversation?

338
00:17:58,827 --> 00:18:01,497
Since the inspection
was interrupted earlier,

339
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:03,832
-we'd like to continue.
-Is there still something else?

340
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:06,960
You mentioned you're engaged.

341
00:18:07,044 --> 00:18:10,255
When and how did you meet?

342
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:11,590
It was fate.

343
00:18:11,673 --> 00:18:14,426
Just like how stones draw people in,
we were drawn to each other--

344
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:15,928
A dating app.

345
00:18:16,011 --> 00:18:17,012
What?

346
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:20,182
There's an app for celebrities.

347
00:18:20,265 --> 00:18:23,519
We messaged for about a week
and instantly hit it off.

348
00:18:23,602 --> 00:18:24,436
Right?

349
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:28,982
-A dating app?
-That's right.

350
00:18:29,066 --> 00:18:31,902
When did you actually meet in person?

351
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:35,155
-It's as if in a past life we knew--
-Three days ago.

352
00:18:35,739 --> 00:18:37,407
-What?
-What?

353
00:18:37,491 --> 00:18:40,077
I went all the way to Unitia,

354
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:42,204
and that was our first meeting.

355
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:47,042
The moment we met, we both knew
we were the one for each other.

356
00:18:48,627 --> 00:18:49,878
Time doesn't matter in love.

357
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:55,467
They met through an app
and got engaged right away.

358
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:57,761
There is being efficient,
and then there is this.

359
00:18:58,512 --> 00:19:02,474
Both of them got engaged
to Japanese corporate executives

360
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:05,102
and gave them similar rings.

361
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:08,647
These two…

362
00:19:10,315 --> 00:19:11,900
might be in cahoots.

363
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,323
METROPOLITAN POLICE DEPARTMENT

364
00:19:18,407 --> 00:19:21,243
Is the tactical unit still not there?

365
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:22,619
Pacing around

366
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:25,122
won't make them arrive any faster.

367
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:26,874
How can you remain so calm?

368
00:19:26,957 --> 00:19:28,417
It's a hostage situation!
A hostage situation!

369
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:30,752
And it's terrible weather outside.

370
00:19:30,836 --> 00:19:33,422
Everything is completely unexpected.

371
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:37,384
Crises always exceed expectations.

372
00:19:38,302 --> 00:19:40,345
Only our ground staff can deal with it.

373
00:19:41,138 --> 00:19:42,973
All we can do is trust them.

374
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:57,154
Hayami, Mori.

375
00:19:57,237 --> 00:19:58,447
This is Iuchi from Tokyo Police.

376
00:20:00,115 --> 00:20:03,368
The guy named Luca there
and that guy Leon over here

377
00:20:03,452 --> 00:20:06,496
might belong to the same
marriage fraud ring.

378
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:09,875
We checked Leon Araki,

379
00:20:09,958 --> 00:20:13,128
but found no record
of his activity as a gem appraiser.

380
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:16,298
I'm just providing you with info.

381
00:20:16,381 --> 00:20:18,675
The tactical unit arrives in 20 minutes.

382
00:20:19,343 --> 00:20:21,887
Do not provoke the suspect
under any circumstances.

383
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:28,685
Hey. What are you doing?

384
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:37,236
Take it off.

385
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:38,362
You too, off!

386
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:52,334
That was close.

387
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:54,878
Audio is still being picked up.

388
00:20:54,962 --> 00:20:57,547
But they can't contact us now.

389
00:20:59,216 --> 00:21:02,511
From here on, it depends on those two.

390
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:06,890
-Um…
-What is it?

391
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:13,230
Um, Luca, you came to Japan
to study abroad, right?

392
00:21:14,273 --> 00:21:16,191
-Yes.
-That's right.

393
00:21:16,275 --> 00:21:18,110
Obtaining a medical license
in Japan is Luca's dream.

394
00:21:18,902 --> 00:21:21,530
But for a student about to study
abroad long-term,

395
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:23,865
I don't see any study material here.

396
00:21:24,741 --> 00:21:25,826
What?

397
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:29,204
Not a single medical textbook
or reference book.

398
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:34,584
I was planning to get them in Japan.

399
00:21:36,086 --> 00:21:37,546
Is that so?

400
00:21:43,176 --> 00:21:46,054
Regarding your study abroad,
I have a question as well.

401
00:21:46,138 --> 00:21:49,266
Luca, have you already paid
the tuition for your school?

402
00:21:51,101 --> 00:21:53,312
Of course he has. Right?

403
00:21:53,812 --> 00:21:58,525
The documents earlier contained neither
a payment confirmation nor a receipt.

404
00:21:59,151 --> 00:22:01,486
Even an email would be enough.
Do you have anything?

405
00:22:04,114 --> 00:22:05,115
Luca?

406
00:22:06,700 --> 00:22:09,119
If we cannot confirm
the reality of your studies,

407
00:22:09,202 --> 00:22:11,371
we cannot permit entry into the country.

408
00:22:11,455 --> 00:22:13,582
Huh? He can't enter Japan?

409
00:22:15,834 --> 00:22:17,336
That's great news.

410
00:22:18,295 --> 00:22:19,379
You paid it, right?

411
00:22:19,921 --> 00:22:22,591
Luca, check your account.

412
00:22:23,216 --> 00:22:24,593
-Right now?
-Yes.

413
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:26,928
-Here?
-Yes.

414
00:22:30,807 --> 00:22:33,226
-Hey.
-Just give it to me.

415
00:22:37,522 --> 00:22:39,274
Here, open it.

416
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:45,697
21,136 YEN

417
00:22:45,781 --> 00:22:46,656
It's gone.

418
00:22:47,866 --> 00:22:49,367
Why isn't it here?

419
00:22:49,910 --> 00:22:51,995
I'm sure I transferred it here!
Twenty million yen!

420
00:22:54,414 --> 00:22:55,373
T-Twenty million?

421
00:22:55,457 --> 00:22:57,834
That's a massive amount.

422
00:22:57,918 --> 00:23:00,378
Tsuzuki, you gave that much to Luca?

423
00:23:02,839 --> 00:23:04,591
What's wrong with that?

424
00:23:05,383 --> 00:23:07,928
Luca had student loan debt back home

425
00:23:08,011 --> 00:23:10,138
and was about to give up
on becoming a doctor.

426
00:23:10,764 --> 00:23:16,186
That's why I decided to support
his tuition and living expenses.

427
00:23:16,269 --> 00:23:20,065
That's a typical textbook scam.

428
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:26,321
I'm paying for everything.

429
00:23:26,988 --> 00:23:28,323
-What?
-What?

430
00:23:29,032 --> 00:23:32,369
His travel expenses,
living costs in Japan,

431
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:34,579
all of it is paid by me. Right?

432
00:23:34,663 --> 00:23:36,790
It's just a temporary advance.

433
00:23:36,873 --> 00:23:39,751
I happened to tie up my funds
for a major purchase recently.

434
00:23:40,293 --> 00:23:42,629
I hope your work goes smoothly.

435
00:23:42,712 --> 00:23:44,798
Aoi, thank you.

436
00:23:46,299 --> 00:23:48,760
In this case, it's also the woman paying.

437
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:55,559
These two men are looking
more and more similar.

438
00:23:55,642 --> 00:23:57,185
Hey, Luca.

439
00:23:57,269 --> 00:23:58,854
Where did my money go?

440
00:23:59,563 --> 00:24:01,857
Did you splurge it all away or something?

441
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:03,441
Be honest.

442
00:24:09,656 --> 00:24:10,866
Give me that.

443
00:24:12,159 --> 00:24:13,952
Akane? Who's that?

444
00:24:17,122 --> 00:24:20,125
Is she your lover in Japan?

445
00:24:20,917 --> 00:24:23,253
Was she the real reason you came to Japan?

446
00:24:23,837 --> 00:24:26,006
How much longer
are you planning to trick Toko?

447
00:24:26,089 --> 00:24:28,466
-Gunji…
-Um…

448
00:24:29,217 --> 00:24:31,845
I have one request.

449
00:24:36,808 --> 00:24:39,060
I want to inspect
the ingredients of those pills.

450
00:24:40,395 --> 00:24:41,396
The pills?

451
00:24:41,479 --> 00:24:43,899
Yes. The ones Tsuzuki was taking.

452
00:24:44,691 --> 00:24:48,778
I've been wondering the whole time
whether they're really just supplements.

453
00:24:56,161 --> 00:24:57,621
How are you going to inspect them?

454
00:25:01,666 --> 00:25:04,377
Entered the underground passage.
ETA about ten minutes.

455
00:25:04,461 --> 00:25:07,130
Roger that. We've got an entry plan.

456
00:25:11,468 --> 00:25:13,094
This is Matsuyama.

457
00:25:13,178 --> 00:25:16,014
I'm the only one standing
in front of the door.

458
00:25:20,101 --> 00:25:22,437
I am going to open the door now.

459
00:25:23,146 --> 00:25:25,148
Don't try anything funny.

460
00:25:25,899 --> 00:25:26,816
I won't.

461
00:25:31,947 --> 00:25:33,323
Slowly, okay?

462
00:25:34,366 --> 00:25:35,450
Okay.

463
00:25:50,006 --> 00:25:51,675
When am I getting my fountain pen back?

464
00:25:51,758 --> 00:25:54,427
-Leon, please calm down.
-The police are about to come in, right?

465
00:25:54,511 --> 00:25:56,346
-Wait!
-What if it gets scratched?

466
00:25:56,429 --> 00:25:57,764
Police?

467
00:26:01,309 --> 00:26:02,269
Mori.

468
00:26:06,273 --> 00:26:07,899
My goodness.

469
00:26:09,776 --> 00:26:11,027
This is bad.

470
00:26:11,111 --> 00:26:12,487
Why is the police coming?!

471
00:26:13,113 --> 00:26:15,657
So you were using this
to snitch to them after all!

472
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:18,118
-No…
-Don't lie to me, you bastard!

473
00:26:18,201 --> 00:26:22,330
You were pretending to cooperate
just to buy time!

474
00:26:22,414 --> 00:26:24,457
-That's not true. I'm--
-Shut up!

475
00:26:24,541 --> 00:26:26,626
I can't trust any of you anymore!

476
00:26:26,710 --> 00:26:29,045
-Gunji!
-It isn't over yet!

477
00:26:30,630 --> 00:26:31,631
It isn't over?

478
00:26:33,174 --> 00:26:34,384
T-The inspection.

479
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:37,762
There is still a place we haven't checked.

480
00:26:38,722 --> 00:26:39,931
Mori.

481
00:26:46,021 --> 00:26:46,855
Please look.

482
00:26:47,856 --> 00:26:50,191
-Look in this bag.
-What's that?

483
00:26:52,193 --> 00:26:53,361
May I open it?

484
00:26:53,445 --> 00:26:55,363
-Wait--
-Don't move!

485
00:26:57,032 --> 00:26:57,991
Open it.

486
00:27:02,537 --> 00:27:03,747
Pardon me.

487
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:18,345
-"Dear Luca"?
-Give it back!

488
00:27:26,853 --> 00:27:28,229
"To my beloved Luca.

489
00:27:28,313 --> 00:27:31,024
If anything should happen to me,

490
00:27:31,107 --> 00:27:35,904
I bequeath my corporate shares
and all my assets to you,

491
00:27:35,987 --> 00:27:38,698
Luca Bennett."

492
00:27:41,868 --> 00:27:43,495
What is this?

493
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:48,625
Is it a will?

494
00:27:49,167 --> 00:27:53,088
No, there's no date,
so it doesn't seem to be formal.

495
00:27:55,340 --> 00:27:57,092
I was just organizing my feelings

496
00:27:58,134 --> 00:28:00,387
before consulting a lawyer.

497
00:28:00,470 --> 00:28:02,055
Feelings?

498
00:28:03,390 --> 00:28:05,392
Forget about 20 million.

499
00:28:05,475 --> 00:28:08,103
You intended to give
this guy all your assets?

500
00:28:10,105 --> 00:28:12,357
You knew that?

501
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:14,776
When I wrote this, that was my intention.

502
00:28:16,569 --> 00:28:18,071
I wanted to support Luca's dream

503
00:28:19,364 --> 00:28:21,116
and thought of it as proof of love.

504
00:28:23,535 --> 00:28:25,537
But now I don't know anymore.

505
00:28:27,539 --> 00:28:29,416
You didn't pay the tuition.

506
00:28:29,958 --> 00:28:32,710
You won't say where
the 20 million went either.

507
00:28:33,420 --> 00:28:37,549
Nor the real reason you came to Japan.

508
00:28:39,217 --> 00:28:40,301
Hey.

509
00:28:40,969 --> 00:28:42,971
What is the meaning of this, Luca?

510
00:28:52,647 --> 00:28:54,733
The test results
for the medicine just came back.

511
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:58,278
A component called
norglycemide was detected.

512
00:28:59,154 --> 00:29:01,030
Norglycemide.

513
00:29:01,865 --> 00:29:03,158
What's that?

514
00:29:03,241 --> 00:29:05,827
It's certainly not an ingredient
in a beauty supplement.

515
00:29:05,910 --> 00:29:07,871
It strongly affects the body's metabolism,

516
00:29:07,954 --> 00:29:10,665
and if overdosed, carries a risk
of inducing a coma.

517
00:29:10,749 --> 00:29:13,168
Worst case, it could be life-threatening.

518
00:29:13,877 --> 00:29:15,128
Life-threatening?

519
00:29:15,670 --> 00:29:19,674
You weren't just tricking Toko,
you were trying to kill her?

520
00:29:19,758 --> 00:29:21,676
No, I would never--

521
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:23,344
If Toko dies, you get all her assets.

522
00:29:23,428 --> 00:29:26,014
Then, with that Akane woman in Japan…

523
00:29:29,726 --> 00:29:31,728
-Toko…
-Enough!

524
00:29:32,645 --> 00:29:34,814
I was such a fool.

525
00:29:36,107 --> 00:29:38,109
I blindly assumed it was fate.

526
00:29:39,861 --> 00:29:41,237
TO MY BELOVED LUCA

527
00:29:44,866 --> 00:29:46,367
I'm glad I found out…

528
00:29:47,911 --> 00:29:49,370
before it came to this.

529
00:29:55,835 --> 00:29:56,920
Um…

530
00:29:59,339 --> 00:30:01,549
Why did you write

531
00:30:02,926 --> 00:30:04,803
that will?

532
00:30:07,305 --> 00:30:11,184
You said it was "proof of love",

533
00:30:11,768 --> 00:30:15,730
but I don't understand love

534
00:30:15,814 --> 00:30:17,857
very well,

535
00:30:19,150 --> 00:30:20,527
so I wanted you to tell me.

536
00:30:26,991 --> 00:30:28,409
I told you

537
00:30:29,369 --> 00:30:33,665
I collapsed a year ago
in the Unitia Federation, right?

538
00:30:34,707 --> 00:30:39,087
Yes. Luca happened to pass by
and helped you.

539
00:30:40,672 --> 00:30:42,715
I found that out later.

540
00:30:43,383 --> 00:30:44,300
The truth is,

541
00:30:45,009 --> 00:30:47,262
my vision suddenly went dark,

542
00:30:47,804 --> 00:30:49,430
and I lost consciousness right then.

543
00:30:50,431 --> 00:30:51,266
What?

544
00:30:53,142 --> 00:30:54,978
I recovered at first,

545
00:30:56,020 --> 00:30:59,107
but after that,
I kept getting cold sweats,

546
00:30:59,607 --> 00:31:00,567
my hands shook.

547
00:31:02,277 --> 00:31:04,529
I got sick over and over.

548
00:31:05,196 --> 00:31:06,573
Back then,

549
00:31:07,907 --> 00:31:10,660
I seriously thought I might die.

550
00:31:12,078 --> 00:31:13,121
But…

551
00:31:16,583 --> 00:31:21,337
even after helping me,
Luca took care of me.

552
00:31:24,048 --> 00:31:26,009
I wanted to thank him,

553
00:31:26,092 --> 00:31:27,760
so I supported him in my own way.

554
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:30,513
The will was the same.

555
00:31:32,765 --> 00:31:33,892
It felt like…

556
00:31:39,314 --> 00:31:41,149
Luca gave me my life back.

557
00:31:51,701 --> 00:31:54,495
Um, Tsuzuki.

558
00:31:57,248 --> 00:31:59,250
Regarding those symptoms,

559
00:31:59,334 --> 00:32:02,670
did you also experience
palpitations or intense hunger?

560
00:32:03,254 --> 00:32:04,339
I did.

561
00:32:04,839 --> 00:32:05,882
How did you know?

562
00:32:07,091 --> 00:32:08,885
Those are symptoms of hypoglycemia.

563
00:32:08,968 --> 00:32:11,971
The medicine earlier, norglycemide,

564
00:32:12,055 --> 00:32:14,307
acts to raise blood sugar levels.

565
00:32:14,390 --> 00:32:17,602
While dangerous for healthy individuals,
if your blood sugar drops too low,

566
00:32:17,685 --> 00:32:19,729
it serves as medicine to prevent attacks.

567
00:32:20,355 --> 00:32:24,192
Then this guy was trying to…

568
00:32:24,275 --> 00:32:27,153
Rather than trying to kill you,

569
00:32:28,488 --> 00:32:30,990
maybe he was trying to protect you.

570
00:32:34,410 --> 00:32:36,746
Why did you stay silent about that?

571
00:32:38,706 --> 00:32:42,710
Was there a circumstance
that kept you from speaking?

572
00:32:48,174 --> 00:32:49,425
Tell me.

573
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:58,768
Toko.

574
00:33:05,149 --> 00:33:06,484
You have a tumor

575
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:08,945
in your pancreas.

576
00:33:09,862 --> 00:33:11,114
A tumor?

577
00:33:11,739 --> 00:33:13,908
It has already spread to your liver.

578
00:33:14,659 --> 00:33:17,453
It's too advanced to remove surgically.

579
00:33:20,832 --> 00:33:23,918
Is it incurable?

580
00:33:24,627 --> 00:33:28,214
I've tried to tell you many times,
but you said you didn't want to hear it

581
00:33:28,297 --> 00:33:29,924
until things settled down at work.

582
00:33:38,349 --> 00:33:39,892
Toko!

583
00:33:41,394 --> 00:33:43,354
-Toko!
-Are you all right?

584
00:33:47,817 --> 00:33:49,110
Luca.

585
00:33:49,861 --> 00:33:51,237
Toko, can you hear me?

586
00:33:51,320 --> 00:33:52,488
What are those candies?

587
00:33:52,572 --> 00:33:54,240
It's glucose.

588
00:33:55,867 --> 00:33:57,410
Chew them slowly.

589
00:33:58,161 --> 00:34:00,496
Now, let's slow the breathing down.

590
00:34:07,336 --> 00:34:10,465
Breathe out slowly. That's it.

591
00:34:12,050 --> 00:34:13,134
You're okay.

592
00:34:14,469 --> 00:34:15,928
She's calming down.

593
00:34:17,597 --> 00:34:19,766
Let me call the hospital, just to be safe.

594
00:34:20,516 --> 00:34:21,684
The hospital?

595
00:34:25,521 --> 00:34:28,191
Does this "Akane"

596
00:34:29,233 --> 00:34:30,318
refer to the hospital?

597
00:34:31,110 --> 00:34:32,153
Huh?

598
00:34:38,284 --> 00:34:39,786
This is Akane Medical Center.

599
00:34:40,328 --> 00:34:41,996
This is Luca Bennett.

600
00:34:42,080 --> 00:34:44,248
I'm calling again about Toko Tsuzuki.

601
00:34:45,208 --> 00:34:47,460
Please put me through
to her doctor, Shidagama.

602
00:34:47,543 --> 00:34:49,128
So that's what it was.

603
00:34:51,714 --> 00:34:55,134
Then everything was for Toko's sake?

604
00:34:55,218 --> 00:34:57,470
-Her blood pressure has dropped again.
-It appears so.

605
00:34:57,553 --> 00:34:59,430
‎Currently applying first-aid
‎as quickly as I can.

606
00:35:00,223 --> 00:35:03,768
Luca isn't a scammer at all.

607
00:35:03,851 --> 00:35:05,645
He was caring for Toko the whole time.

608
00:35:05,728 --> 00:35:06,646
Iuchi!

609
00:35:07,355 --> 00:35:09,440
The tactical unit has arrived.

610
00:35:15,822 --> 00:35:16,781
What's the situation?

611
00:35:16,864 --> 00:35:19,200
Inside the secondary room,
one suspect, four hostages.

612
00:35:19,283 --> 00:35:20,827
-Get into position.
-Yes, sir.

613
00:35:22,411 --> 00:35:24,330
Could you hold off for a bit?

614
00:35:25,164 --> 00:35:27,333
I am Iuchi
from the International Crime Division.

615
00:35:28,709 --> 00:35:30,169
The situation inside has changed.

616
00:35:30,753 --> 00:35:32,588
The suspect is starting to calm down.

617
00:35:32,672 --> 00:35:35,591
Right now, Gate 24 staff

618
00:35:35,675 --> 00:35:37,552
are risking their lives
to resolve things inside.

619
00:35:38,177 --> 00:35:39,971
I understand. Thank you very much.

620
00:35:43,182 --> 00:35:44,183
Luca.

621
00:35:46,978 --> 00:35:48,855
What about the money I gave you?

622
00:35:54,652 --> 00:35:55,820
It seems

623
00:35:56,946 --> 00:36:00,783
all of it went toward
your medical expenses, Tsuzuki.

624
00:36:03,953 --> 00:36:06,289
Medication, consultation requests

625
00:36:06,372 --> 00:36:10,376
to the medical center,
preparations for tests and treatment.

626
00:36:11,002 --> 00:36:12,545
Including future expenses,

627
00:36:13,296 --> 00:36:16,883
he likely didn't spend
a single yen on himself.

628
00:36:18,801 --> 00:36:20,803
One more thing.

629
00:36:21,888 --> 00:36:22,972
Luca.

630
00:36:23,973 --> 00:36:27,977
You got a job at Akane Medical Center,
didn't you?

631
00:36:28,060 --> 00:36:28,936
What?

632
00:36:32,982 --> 00:36:36,694
Helping foreign patients
and assisting with medical examinations.

633
00:36:37,862 --> 00:36:38,905
Of course,

634
00:36:38,988 --> 00:36:42,783
you will need to pass through Immigration
again, with the proper procedures.

635
00:36:46,954 --> 00:36:48,080
Then,

636
00:36:49,582 --> 00:36:52,293
for your living expenses in Japan,

637
00:36:52,376 --> 00:36:55,004
you intend to earn them yourself?

638
00:36:57,048 --> 00:36:58,549
Why?

639
00:36:58,633 --> 00:37:00,092
Like I said before,

640
00:37:01,594 --> 00:37:03,971
you've always been there for me.

641
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:06,599
Now I want to be there for you.

642
00:37:11,312 --> 00:37:12,980
I don't want your inheritance.

643
00:37:14,315 --> 00:37:16,484
You don't have to stay with me.

644
00:37:19,237 --> 00:37:20,404
Please…

645
00:37:23,866 --> 00:37:25,701
put your health first.

646
00:37:49,809 --> 00:37:50,643
Toko.

647
00:37:52,979 --> 00:37:55,147
I didn't notice a single thing.

648
00:37:59,235 --> 00:38:00,611
I'm sorry.

649
00:38:22,466 --> 00:38:23,843
This is Hayami.

650
00:38:25,678 --> 00:38:28,931
Gunji has surrendered his weapon.
He has no intent to resist.

651
00:38:30,516 --> 00:38:31,559
I am opening the door.

652
00:38:40,526 --> 00:38:41,736
On your knees!

653
00:38:41,819 --> 00:38:42,820
-Search him.
-Roger.

654
00:38:42,903 --> 00:38:44,322
On the floor!

655
00:38:45,489 --> 00:38:46,824
Nothing on him.

656
00:39:05,926 --> 00:39:10,222
Apparently, the person who reported
a scammer on this flight was Gunji.

657
00:39:10,306 --> 00:39:11,682
Gunji?

658
00:39:11,766 --> 00:39:14,185
Thanks to that,
we were able to get this far.

659
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:16,729
Well, in reality,

660
00:39:16,812 --> 00:39:19,148
-the actual scammer was someone else.
-Look!

661
00:39:19,231 --> 00:39:20,107
This scratch!

662
00:39:20,191 --> 00:39:22,234
What have you done?

663
00:39:22,318 --> 00:39:25,488
We need to confiscate it as a weapon.

664
00:39:25,571 --> 00:39:28,240
Do you realize how valuable this item is?

665
00:39:31,202 --> 00:39:34,080
That fountain pen is not worth that much.

666
00:39:34,163 --> 00:39:35,456
Excuse me.

667
00:39:37,958 --> 00:39:41,045
Underneath the scratch,
another metal is visible.

668
00:39:41,128 --> 00:39:44,673
This is not solid gold.
It's plated on the surface.

669
00:39:45,299 --> 00:39:47,718
The decorative stone is also just glass.

670
00:39:49,428 --> 00:39:52,473
Also, we heard from Luca.

671
00:39:52,556 --> 00:39:54,308
Before coming here,

672
00:39:54,392 --> 00:39:57,436
you sold him a ring, right?

673
00:39:58,104 --> 00:40:00,481
You claimed it was a real sapphire.

674
00:40:00,564 --> 00:40:02,775
We have a lot of questions to ask you.

675
00:40:03,484 --> 00:40:04,735
Onodera.

676
00:40:07,696 --> 00:40:09,740
Most likely, that ring as well.

677
00:40:10,449 --> 00:40:12,243
I know.

678
00:40:12,910 --> 00:40:14,787
I can tell it's a fake.

679
00:40:15,788 --> 00:40:16,997
You knew?

680
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:20,042
I called myself a CEO,

681
00:40:20,126 --> 00:40:22,294
but my company is small.
I'm the only employee.

682
00:40:23,170 --> 00:40:24,004
What?

683
00:40:24,505 --> 00:40:28,175
I want to hire people,
but things haven't gone well.

684
00:40:28,259 --> 00:40:31,720
So, perhaps you dated Leon…

685
00:40:32,471 --> 00:40:36,100
Not to find a marriage partner,
but an employee?

686
00:40:37,309 --> 00:40:38,561
Aoi?

687
00:40:44,442 --> 00:40:47,695
I knew you were full of lies.

688
00:40:49,488 --> 00:40:52,158
But your smooth talking and nerve,

689
00:40:52,241 --> 00:40:54,243
those at least were real.

690
00:40:55,369 --> 00:40:57,496
Tell everything to the police

691
00:40:58,456 --> 00:41:01,709
and make amends for what you've done.

692
00:41:02,835 --> 00:41:03,836
And then,

693
00:41:05,796 --> 00:41:08,382
if you intend to turn your life around…

694
00:41:10,342 --> 00:41:11,719
come to me.

695
00:41:16,474 --> 00:41:17,766
What's your answer?

696
00:41:21,103 --> 00:41:22,104
Yes.

697
00:41:27,234 --> 00:41:29,820
-Well then, right this way.
-Okay.

698
00:41:30,529 --> 00:41:33,240
May we talk to you as well, Onodera?

699
00:41:33,324 --> 00:41:34,200
Yes.

700
00:41:40,414 --> 00:41:41,457
Tsuzuki.

701
00:41:42,666 --> 00:41:44,752
Thank you for your help.

702
00:41:48,255 --> 00:41:51,383
I will pay Luca's tuition immediately.

703
00:41:51,467 --> 00:41:56,305
That will satisfy
the purpose of entry, right?

704
00:41:56,388 --> 00:41:57,223
Toko.

705
00:41:58,224 --> 00:41:59,058
‎Yes.

706
00:42:00,434 --> 00:42:01,602
Thank you very much.

707
00:42:08,776 --> 00:42:10,236
APPROVED BY IMMIGRATION

708
00:42:10,319 --> 00:42:11,529
Good luck.

709
00:42:11,612 --> 00:42:12,655
‎Thank you.

710
00:42:13,656 --> 00:42:15,658
-Here you are.
-Thank you very much.

711
00:42:18,035 --> 00:42:20,412
Welcome to Japan.

712
00:42:23,541 --> 00:42:24,917
‎Thank you.

713
00:42:36,595 --> 00:42:37,846
So this is love.

714
00:42:48,983 --> 00:42:51,986
-I'm glad they resolved it safely.
-Yes.

715
00:42:52,069 --> 00:42:53,779
Thanks to the brave people on the ground.

716
00:42:55,072 --> 00:42:57,866
You really seem to trust Gate 24.

717
00:42:58,492 --> 00:43:00,995
Yes. It's the team I built, after all.

718
00:43:01,870 --> 00:43:03,622
Your team, huh?

719
00:43:05,666 --> 00:43:09,545
I hope that trust is never betrayed.

720
00:43:10,212 --> 00:43:11,088
Goodbye.

721
00:43:44,622 --> 00:43:46,290
It's been a while, huh?

722
00:43:47,499 --> 00:43:48,709
What's going on?

723
00:43:49,501 --> 00:43:50,794
I have a favor to ask.

724
00:43:51,420 --> 00:43:54,173
I want you to look for a spy.

725
00:43:55,507 --> 00:43:56,425
What do you mean?

726
00:43:56,508 --> 00:43:59,345
We received a report
that for the past two months,

727
00:43:59,428 --> 00:44:02,723
there have been people involved
with terrorists and extremists

728
00:44:02,806 --> 00:44:04,350
entering the country at a rapid scale.

729
00:44:04,433 --> 00:44:08,020
Gate 24 has become
a shortcut for terrorists.

730
00:44:08,812 --> 00:44:11,148
There's a spy in Gate 24?

731
00:44:13,025 --> 00:44:14,234
I want you to look for that spy.

732
00:44:15,027 --> 00:44:16,362
I'm counting on you.

733
00:44:33,921 --> 00:44:35,130
Mori.

734
00:44:37,633 --> 00:44:38,884
Oh my.

735
00:44:44,014 --> 00:44:44,848
‎AT LAST, THE FINAL CHAPTER!

736
00:44:44,932 --> 00:44:46,975
‎Inspection is temporarily halted
‎at the moment.

737
00:44:47,059 --> 00:44:48,560
‎-I'm a doctor.
‎-Was it an accident,

738
00:44:48,644 --> 00:44:50,521
‎-or on purpose?
‎-‎Someone among us

739
00:44:50,604 --> 00:44:53,065
‎is in direct contact with a person
‎suspected of being a spy.

740
00:44:53,148 --> 00:44:56,568
‎If there really is a spy at Gate 24…

741
00:44:56,652 --> 00:44:58,904
‎-This is…
‎-Oh my.

742
00:44:58,987 --> 00:44:59,863
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
